  "references": {
    "1": {
      "note": "The Manager starts Worker, Reviewer and Curator together through one role_start_set; Worker opens immediately, the other seats are held unless first Reviewer work is supplied. Public messaging takes a unique live seat, refuses ambiguity, and holds behind already-held messages when a start, permission prompt or non-steerable turn prevents delivery. Permission decisions are never answered by transport; the upward notice names the role/task/agent/permission, and the product delivers held work when admissible without sender resubmission. CODE and MEMORY lanes keep separate counts; the settings limit and recorded architect/developer authority govern extra rounds. Direct peer packages are not relayed by Manager.",
